3. Permitted operational adoption

Subject to this license, you may copy, modify, execute, and distribute the
Materials and derivative versions for systems operated by Dots within
OpenAI-operated ChatGPT, and for OpenAI Codex workflows directly supporting
those systems. Supporting workflows include authoring, building, testing,
validation, debugging, deployment, and maintenance.

A permitted system may include websites, surfaces, services, databases,
deterministic automation, local programs, and other infrastructure deployed
on Vercel, another hosting service, or local computers. The hosting location
does not determine eligibility. Human users and administrators may interact
with, administer, and use the outputs of a permitted system. Ordinary users
of a website or service need not themselves use a Dot.

The operational assistant role must remain with OpenAI ChatGPT Dots, with
OpenAI Codex permitted in the supporting role described above. You may not
use the Materials to implement, equip, or operate a non-OpenAI assistant as
an operational participant, substitute operator, or supervising agent of the
system. Routing such an assistant through a Dot, proxy, hosting service, or
OpenAI API does not make it eligible. Using an OpenAI model or API alone
does not qualify an otherwise ineligible assistant as a Dot or Codex.

Development tools and automated tests may run outside ChatGPT and Codex
when directly supporting a permitted system. This permission does not
authorize an independent operational adoption by another assistant.

"Operational adoption" means incorporating the Materials into an agent's
or application's active instructions, implementation, or operating workflow.
Other operational adoption requires separate permission from the applicable
rights holder.

